{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1553569-power-tag-homebrew","id":1553569,"title":"Power Tag Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-31T15:35:03-07:00","id":1553569,"title":"Power Tag Homebrew","content":"So, I've done some thinking on some custom Power Tags, since I'm designing a sand-bending Nova and I wanted some stuff to accomodate that. Anyone mind taking a look at these to see if they're okay?<br /> <br /> <b>Evident (-1 to -2):</b> With this tag, a power leaves behind evidence of its use which is specific enough to give any investigators a clue as to who used it. Either as a result of unique residue, or distinguishable blast marks, clues point to the Nova having used their abilities, and what kind of powers were employed. At -1, characters trying to find clues of the Nova's involvement in a situation, the direction they left in or to uncover how their powers work, gain +3 Enhancement to the roll. At -2, no rolls are necessary, the evidence left behind is obvious enough that the Nova can be quickly identified.<br /> <br /> Example: Sandman, the sand-manipulating Nova, has the power Flight 3 - 1 (Surfing). This means that he can fly on top of a solid platform made of blue sand at Speed Scale 3. If he has the Evident (-1) tag, his sand platform leaves behind a visible trail of blue sand, allowing others to track where he's gone. With Evident (-2), the trail is so large and visible to the naked eye that a detective following his trail doesn't even need to roll to locate him.<br /> <br /> <b>Hazardous (-2):</b> With this tag, a power harms the user in order to function. A Quantum Construct can only be created from a haemokinetic's own blood, or a Nova with a radiation-beam isn't as immune to its effects as they would like. Whenever the tagged power is used, the Nova suffers an Injury Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Obscuring (+1):</b> Quantum Field Only. When this tag is applied to the power, it covers the Nova's body, obscuring the details from view. Any attempts to see what's underneath suffer a 3-point Complication. Failing to pay off this Complication results in incorrect information, such as an observer believing that the man in encompassing shadowy armor is taller, shorter or otherwise different from how he actually looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}